Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:49:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] auth: accept the api_key query parameter without legacy
 authorization

Intent: 12.1 switches EnableLegacyAuthorization off on upgrade (the
DisableLegacyAuthorization migration), after which AuthorizationContext
reads only ApiKey from the query string. The official 12.1 jellyfin-web
still opens its WebSocket as socket?api_key= and builds the Download
link with api_key, so every web session had its socket refused with 403
(no remote control, SyncPlay or live updates) and Download failed.
api_key is now read like ApiKey whatever the legacy setting. It is the
same token in the same place, so nothing new is accepted; the
X-Emby-Token and X-MediaBrowser-Token headers and the Emby scheme stay
behind the setting.
Proven with the image: the smoke asserts /Users/Me?api_key= answers 200
while the X-Emby-Token header is still refused.
Drop when: jellyfin-web sends ApiKey on its socket and Download URLs, or
upstream reads api_key again.

Patch: 0024
---
 .../Security/AuthorizationContext.cs                           | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Jellyfin.Server.Implementations/Security/AuthorizationContext.cs b/Jellyfin.Server.Implementations/Security/AuthorizationContext.cs
index 8657cb7..ebe76a2 100644
--- a/Jellyfin.Server.Implementations/Security/AuthorizationContext.cs
+++ b/Jellyfin.Server.Implementations/Security/AuthorizationContext.cs
@@ -105,7 +105,8 @@ namespace Jellyfin.Server.Implementations.Security
                 token = queryString["ApiKey"];
             }
 
-            if (_configurationManager.Configuration.EnableLegacyAuthorization && string.IsNullOrEmpty(token))
+            // The 12.1 web client still sends api_key on the socket URL and Download links.
+            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(token))
             {
                 token = queryString["api_key"];
             }
